WEBVTT

NOTE The General (1926) - Riah TV captions

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:09.750
Joseph M. Schenck presents
Buster Keaton in "The General".
A United Artists Production

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:22.934
Adapted by Al Boasberg and
Charles Smith. Photographed by
Dev Jennings and Bert Haines.
Technical Director: Fred

00:00:22.944 --> 00:00:27.500
Gabourie. Lighting Effects:
Denver Harmon

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:35.708
The cast: Annabelle Lee, Marion
Mack. Captain Anderson, Glen
Cavender. General Thatcher, Jim
Farley. A Southern General,

00:00:35.718 --> 00:00:41.356
Frederick Vroom. Her father,
Charles Smith. Her brother,
Frank Barnes. Three Union
Generals: Joe Keaton, Mike

00:00:41.366 --> 00:00:43.750
Donlin, Tom Nawn. Johnnie Gray,
Buster Keaton.

00:00:44.250 --> 00:01:00.500
The Western and Atlantic Flyer
speeding into Marietta, Ga., in
the Spring of 1861.

00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:04.700
[music]

00:01:56.750 --> 00:02:05.250
There were two loves in
his life. His engine,

00:04:12.750 --> 00:04:15.000
"Fort Sumter has
been fired upon."

00:04:18.250 --> 00:04:20.000
"Then the war is here."

00:04:22.250 --> 00:04:25.500
"Yes, dad, and I'm going to be
one of the first to enlist."

00:04:52.250 --> 00:04:55.000
"Aren't you going to enlist?"

00:05:49.750 --> 00:05:51.500
"Your name?"

00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:54.750
"Johnnie Gray."

00:05:57.500 --> 00:05:59.250
"Occupation?"

00:06:00.750 --> 00:06:04.500
"Engineer on the Western
and Atlantic Railroad."

00:06:20.250 --> 00:06:24.500
"Don't enlist him. He is more
valuable to the South as an
engineer."

00:06:31.500 --> 00:06:33.750
"We can't use you."

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:43.500
"William Brown."

00:07:45.750 --> 00:07:47.500
"Occupation?"

00:07:49.750 --> 00:07:51.500
"Bartender."

00:08:43.750 --> 00:08:46.500
"If you lose this
war don't blame me."

00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:33.000
"Did Johnnie enlist?"

00:09:37.250 --> 00:09:40.250
"He didn't even get in line."

00:09:47.250 --> 00:09:48.750
"He's a disgrace to the South."

00:10:13.500 --> 00:10:15.750
"Why didn't you enlist?"

00:10:18.750 --> 00:10:20.250
"They wouldn't take me."

00:10:25.750 --> 00:10:31.250
"Please don't lie. I don't want
you to speak to me again until
you are in uniform."

00:10:58.750 --> 00:11:08.750
A year later. In a Union
encampment just North of
Chattanooga.

00:11:13.750 --> 00:11:17.750
General Thatcher, and his
chief spy, Captain Anderson.

00:11:21.750 --> 00:11:31.750
"I know every foot of this
railroad from Marietta to
Chattanooga, and with ten picked
men I cannot fail."

00:11:37.250 --> 00:11:47.000
"We will enter the South as
civilians coming from the
neutral state of Kentucky to
join the Southern cause."

00:12:18.750 --> 00:12:26.750
"Then the day you steal the
train I will have General Parker
advance to meet you."

00:12:43.500 --> 00:12:50.250
"As soon as I arrive I will let
you know how seriously father is
wounded."

00:13:23.250 --> 00:13:25.750
"Big Shanty. Twenty
minutes for dinner."

00:17:08.500 --> 00:17:13.500
"Three men stole my General.
I think they are deserters."

00:19:04.500 --> 00:19:07.000
"Why not stop and fight them?"

00:19:10.750 --> 00:19:14.750
"I'm afraid they have
us greatly outnumbered."

00:28:09.500 --> 00:28:14.500
The Southern army facing
Chattanooga is ordered to
retreat.

00:29:18.250 --> 00:29:21.500
General Parker's victorious
Northern army advancing.

00:30:53.250 --> 00:30:56.750
"There is only one
man on that engine."

00:31:43.000 --> 00:31:51.250
In the enemy's country,
hopelessly lost, helplessly cold
and horribly hungry.

00:33:06.250 --> 00:33:16.530
"At nine o'clock tomorrow
morning our supply trains will
meet and unite with General
Parker's army at the Rock River

00:33:16.540 --> 00:33:17.250
bridge."

00:33:19.750 --> 00:33:29.500
"Then the army, backed by our
supply trains, will advance for
a surprise attack on the rebels'
left flank."

00:33:33.250 --> 00:33:40.750
"Once our trains and troops
cross that bridge, nothing on
earth can stop us."

00:34:21.750 --> 00:34:32.000
"This girl was in the baggage
car when we stole the train, so
I thought it best to hold her."

00:39:39.000 --> 00:39:45.000
"We had better stay here until
daybreak to see where we are."

00:39:50.500 --> 00:39:59.750
"It was so brave of you to risk
your life, coming into the
enemy's country, just to save
me."

00:41:35.750 --> 00:41:44.000
"We've got to get back to our
lines somehow and warn them of
this coming attack."

00:44:54.750 --> 00:45:04.250
"I will get that spy before he
reaches the Southern lines. You
follow with the supply trains as
planned."

00:47:43.000 --> 00:47:45.500
"We must pick up more firewood."

00:57:54.500 --> 00:57:57.250
The Rock River bridge.

00:58:18.750 --> 00:58:23.750
The Northern division nearing
the bridge to meet the supply
trains.

01:05:04.750 --> 01:05:10.000
"That bridge is not burned
enough to stop you, and my men
will ford the river."

01:10:14.500 --> 01:10:20.500
Heroes of the day.

01:12:44.500 --> 01:12:46.250
"Is that your uniform?"

01:12:53.000 --> 01:12:55.250
"I had to wear it to
get through the lines."

01:12:57.750 --> 01:12:59.000
"Take it off!"

01:14:01.250 --> 01:14:02.750
"Enlist the Lieutenant."

01:14:10.250 --> 01:14:11.500
"Occupation?"

01:14:14.250 --> 01:14:15.750
"Soldier."

